 r/register/WN_ZyvUqvrWTW22x4eJHWMkBw\n\nIn 2018\, during her brief respite
  of freedom between two decade-long prison sentences\, Mahvash Sabet asked
  Bahiyyih Nakhjavani and Azita Mottahedeh to work on her memoirs and make 
 a book that could convey her story in English. They set to work\, with Mot
 tahedeh translating the Persian original\, word for word\, and Nakhjavani 
 attempting to structure a narrative from the more than 750 pages of a harr
 owing and uplifting testimony which Sabet smuggled out of prison over the 
 years.\n\n“In this discussion\, we will explore the decisions involved a
 nd the methods followed in the course of creating this book\, as well as t
 he distinctive characteristics of Mahvash Sabet's style\, tone and intent\
 , which we hope have survived the translation.  We will share the ways in 
 which this prison memoir may be different from others and at the same time
  how it seems to bear witness to the many which might never be written.  A
 bove all we will try to share Mahvash’s extraordinary capacity to transf
 orm despair into hope\, confinement into freedom\, and estrangement and is
 olation into a boundless compassion towards others.”\n\nBahiyyih Nakhjav
 ani was born in Iran\, raised in Uganda\, and educated in the UK and the U
 S. She received her preliminary degrees in English Literature from the Uni
 versity of York in the UK\, and completed her doctorate at UMass\, Amherst
 \, in the US\, as well as being awarded an honorary doctorate by the Unive
 rsity of Liège in Belgium. In addition to teaching literature and creativ
